{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Two shoulder-pieces, etc.</b> The apron below, and the band of the ephod — that is the girdle — and joined to it above, like a woman's apron. From the priest's back they were joined in the band as two pieces like two broad straps, one opposite each shoulder, and they rise upon his two shoulders until they fold over to the front, opposite the chest, and by their attachment to the rings of the breastplate they are held from the front opposite his heart so they do not fall — as is explained in the matter. And they would rise and go along his shoulders, and the two shoham stones set in them — one in each one." "<b>To its two ends.</b> To the width of the ephod — for its width was only opposite the priest's back, and its height up to opposite the elbows, which they call קודי\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז — as it says: ״לֹא יַחְגְּרוּ בַיָּזַע״ (Ezekiel 44): they do not gird at the place of sweating — neither above their elbows nor below their waists, but opposite their elbows." "<b>And you shall join.</b> The ephod with those two shoulder-pieces of the ephod — he shall join them with a needle below, in the band; and he shall not weave them with it but weave it separately and afterward join them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "the la'az קודי\"ש is Old French codeches / coudes, 'elbows'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:08.782687625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}